  "description": "Continuous camera recording on Linux devices with MediaMTX: installs and supervises MediaMTX as a systemd service at runtime, records RTSP streams (resolved over ONVIF) into fixed-length fMP4 segments with retention and a free-space guard, optionally on a USB disk, and cuts event clips (e.g. 45 s before and after a parking event) from the continuous recording. Camera stream and encoder settings (resolution, bitrate, fps, GOP) are set over ONVIF to control file size. No dependency on FAS - usable from device-side apps.",
